 357:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Control.c **** /*******************************************************************************
 358:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Control.c **** * Function Name: CapSense_ProcessWidget
 359:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Control.c **** ****************************************************************************//**
 360:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Control.c **** *
 361:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Control.c **** * \brief
 362:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Control.c **** *  Performs full data processing of the specified widget if it is enabled.
 363:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Control.c **** *
 364:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Control.c **** * \details
 365:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Control.c **** *  This function performs exactly the same tasks as
 366:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Control.c **** *  CapSense_ProcessAllWidgets(), but only for a specified widget. This
 367:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Control.c **** *  function can be used along with the CapSense_SetupWidget() and
 368:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Control.c **** *  CapSense_Scan() functions to scan and process data for a specific
 369:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Control.c **** *  widget. This function should be called only after all the sensors in the
 370:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Control.c **** *  widgets are scanned. A disabled widget is not processed by this function.
